# The e1000e card with real traffic: an address from DHCP, pings, and a TCP
# transfer larger than both rings (drivers todo, item N1).
@net
@tcp
@e1000e
$ net dhcp
~ ^address 10\.0\.2\.15/24 \(DHCP\)
$ ping -c 3 10.0.2.2
~ ^32 bytes from 10\.0\.2\.2: seq=1 ttl=\d+ time=[\d.]+ ms$
~ ^32 bytes from 10\.0\.2\.2: seq=3 ttl=\d+ time=[\d.]+ ms$
3 sent, 3 received, 0% loss
$ nc {once} hello over e1000e
you said: hello over e1000e
$ nc {lines} go
line 001 of 300 ==============================
line 150 of 300 ==============================
line 300 of 300 ==============================
(the other side closed the connection)
$ net
card:    e1000e (Intel 82574L)
link:    up
chip:    1000 Mb/s, full duplex
